body: "## Summary\n\nWith `--include-empty`, pm-changelog renders an empty `## Unreleased` / `No changes.` section only when HEAD is already tagged. A release writes CHANGELOG.md before it creates its tag, so the committed file can never contain that section. As soon as the tag exists, `--check` with the same flags regenerates it and refuses the committed file:\n\n```\n--- committed CHANGELOG.md\n+++ generated\n@@\n # Changelog\n\n-## 2026.11.11 - 2026-11-11\n+## Unreleased\n+\n+No changes.\n+\n+## 2026.11.11 - 2026-11-11\n```\n\n## Reproduction\n\nReproduced on 2026-11-10 with pm-changelog 2026.11.6 in a pm-slack checkout:\n\n1. Set package.json to the next version and run the release writer (`--mode replace --output CHANGELOG.md --all-release-tags --include-empty --release-version-from-package --date-from-version …`), then commit.\n2. Tag that commit (`git tag v<version>`).\n3. Run the same command with `--check`: it reports \"Changelog is out of date\", with the diff above.\n\n## Impact across the fleet\n\n- After every release, main's committed CHANGELOG.md fails CI's `changelog:check` until some PR regenerates it. Agent PRs regenerate, so they pass.\n- Dependabot PRs never regenerate, so they fail \"Verify generated changelog\" or the release gate until someone pushes a regeneration commit. On 2026-11-10 this blocked pm-jira (#196-#199), pm-evidence#47, pm-brief#212, pm-gantt-chart#222 and others. pm-jira#196's diff was exactly this `+## Unreleased / No changes.` hunk.\n- pm-todos and pm-slack mains currently start with `## Unreleased` / `No changes.` because a later PR regenerated them.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe output must not depend on whether the release commit is tagged yet. Either:\n\n- **(preferred)** `--include-empty` applies to tag sections only, and an empty Unreleased section is never rendered; or\n- the pre-tag writer renders the same empty Unreleased section the post-tag check expects.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A test runs the writer at a pending version, commits, tags, and then runs `--check` with the same flags: it passes with and without `--include-empty`.\n- The same holds for an itemless (Dependabot-only) window and for a window with released items.\n- A release note in the changelog explains that callers' committed changelogs lose the empty Unreleased block on their next regeneration.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-11-10T21:32:09Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-changelog#333 - Keep changelog checks stable after empty release tags [closed]\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!"
